{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/654826-using-a-deceived-for-crone-drama","id":654826,"title":"Using a Deceived for Crone drama.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-07T00:10:32-07:00","id":654826,"title":"Using a Deceived for Crone drama.","content":"This has been stewing in my head for a while but I've been toying with the idea of using a Deceived as a interesting setup to split the Crone faction of the city. Deceived is part of the Keeper and is currently dealing with how to deal with this newly formed vampire cult while fighting off the &quot;purist&quot; crone group.<br /> <br /> Does the Deceived's cult merit still work even if the member is Kindred rather than mortal? or will that require some reworking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T01:05:43-07:00","id":654870,"title":"","content":"Officially, sure, there's no reason why a vampire can't have the deceived cultist merit.<br /> <br /> However, that might be because mummy is first edition, if it were second edition deceived cultist might very well be a supernatural merit. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean you might not want to rework it anyway. For example, having an essence pool and a blood pool is kind of wonky, you might want to make the numina blood powered instead, for example.<br /> <br /> Have you considered incorporating the Followers of Seth mekhet cult into this scenario? Egyptian origin, and they have an ethos that I could see working for the deceived, considering their feelings for the Judges. <br /> <br /> Although I can't help but think that the other style of blood magic would be more appropriate for a mummy crossover, I can't think of any theban sorcery users that would be appropriate, well I suppose the Architects with their gilded cage discipline, but they aren't likely to have much to with the acolytes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:28:25-07:00","id":659256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/654826-using-a-deceived-for-crone-drama?p=654870#post654870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially, sure, there's no reason why a vampire can't have the deceived cultist merit.<br /> <br /> However, that might be because mummy is first edition, if it were second edition deceived cultist might very well be a supernatural merit.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean you might not want to rework it anyway. For example, having an essence pool and a blood pool is kind of wonky, you might want to make the numina blood powered instead, for example.<br /> <br /> Have you considered incorporating the Followers of Seth mekhet cult into this scenario? Egyptian origin, and they have an ethos that I could see working for the deceived, considering their feelings for the Judges.<br /> <br /> Although I can't help but think that the other style of blood magic would be more appropriate for a mummy crossover, I can't think of any theban sorcery users that would be appropriate, well I suppose the Architects with their gilded cage discipline, but they aren't likely to have much to with the acolytes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have looked into the Seth shadow cult but find the ethos clashing a bit with in some parts. The cult as a whole seems like something that would put the Decieved down and cut off it's head. However, that being said, I can work with the mechanics for them without them actually being the cult of Seth.<br /> <br /> Another interesting thing is to have the Kindred in the cult become Hollow and have their Ka flown free, no matter what clan they belong to which would blow any Mekhet's mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}